  <data name="Rt_Apps_Note" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Processes with the same name are added up as one app; the number in parentheses is how many processes it has. CPU is a share of the whole PC based on CPU time (% Processor Time), so it can read lower than Task Manager while boosting. GPU is the busiest engine each process uses. Reads and writes include files, devices and network traffic, so they do not match Task Manager's Disk column. Protected processes are counted too: these values come from performance counters and need no access to the processes themselves.</value>
  </data>
